    "features": [
      "Native hiding commitments, full claimed values and masking suffixes independently match upstream CPU hiding PCS.",
      "Complete native opening proofs pass unchanged CPU PCS verification with production wallet and recursive FRI parameters.",
      "Public and private preprocessing at the upstream round index; four native quotient chunks; mixed-height original inputs; nonzero point offsets and repeated points.",
      "CPU verifier rejects altered masking values and shapes, authenticated original rows and claimed public values.",
      "Aggregate host allowance boundary, invalid hiding geometry, overflowing/out-of-bounds points and retained device pressure fail before mutating state.",
      "Failures after observation/reduction, an unwind and an evaluation point on the coset retire all original randomness/salts, FRI salts and transcript aliases.",
      "Retained openings preserve their evaluated points/values; a failed consumer retires source families and all later aliases reject consumption.",
      "Successful execution and failed attempts release all intermediate device allocations."
    ]
  },
  "admission": {
    "max_original_commitments": 256,
    "max_matrices_per_commitment": 256,
    "max_matrices_per_height": 256,
    "max_points_per_matrix": 32,
    "max_log_height": 25,
    "host": "Checked aggregate raw/typed claimed values, nested metadata and complete FRI host storage before observation.",
    "device": "Preflight all retained points/evaluations and reduction accumulator/scratch peaks. Later FRI stages retain their own admission and the outer PCS attempt retires every family on failure."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This qualifies the native hiding PCS opening wrapper over existing native commitments, not a complete wallet/recursive STARK proof or a selected CUDA proving backend.",
    "Standalone randomization-polynomial commitments, remaining proof stages, complete PCS/backend wiring, execution receipts and worker/pool integration remain outstanding.",
    "No performance or transaction-throughput measurement is claimed by this checkpoint.",
    "CUDA execution is qualified only on the desktop RTX 5080. V100, multi-device ownership rejection and Metal execution remain unqualified.",
    "Deterministic RNGs are test-only. Exact wire comparisons use zero-PoW settings because parallel upstream grinding may choose another valid witness; production-PoW cases use the unchanged CPU verifier.",
    "The intentional missing-kernel test runs outside sanitizers. All five opt-in primitive benchmarks are excluded from correctness/sanitizer runs."
  ],
  "qualification_note": "The initial development build and all six PCS tests passed. The stream opening tests passed all 12 tests on the first run, but the controller expected 10; the corrected 12-test focused rerun also passed. The earlier successful PCS and FRI checks were preserved. Qualification freezes every source file and the final staged source must match those hashes. GPU execution is serial with 3 GiB RAM, zero swap, four CPUs and 96 tasks; the stream build has 6 GiB RAM and one build job.",
